dle mouth) - so **trim your audio to `seconds`**. Longer audio = chain segments: feed this flow's output IMAGE batch into a second `WanInfiniteTalkToVideo`'s **`previous_frames`** (the official extend pattern); each continuation advances `length - motion_frame_count` frames (72 = 2.88 s at defaults - drop the node's `trim_image` leading frames when stitching), not a full segment. For real use reach for `scripts/talk_chain.py` instead of hand-wiring: it plans full chunks plus a trimmed last chunk from the audio duration, assembles in latent space, and muxes once (measured E21: 8.8 s -> 221 frames exact in 606 s). `single_speaker` needs no masks (masks are the two-speaker mode's region control). The patch loads through `ModelPatchLoader` from `models/model_patches/`.\n**Siblings:** `wan-animate-motion.json` (S15) drives motion from a *video*; this flow drives it from *audio*.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S32** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E15** in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*"
